    # v391 (2026-10-07) -- THE STATUS OF THE PROOF: proved; the refused confirmation is accreditation, not validity. The operator's words VERBATIM (checked against
    # the text embedded by sha256); numbers READ from the record estatuto_da_prova_v391 (which reads them from the core at every rite); the period sentences stay, with an erratum beside.
    _ep391 = core.get("estatuto_da_prova_v391") or {}
    _k391 = _ep391.get("prova_1_kernel") or {}
    _r391 = _ep391.get("prova_2_ritos") or {}
    _g391 = (_ep391.get("prova_3_gpu") or {}).get("numeros") or {}
    _h391 = _r391.get("razao_de_hubble") or {}
    _v391 = _r391.get("piso_dos_vazios") or {}
    _e391 = _r391.get("rotas_do_eco_fora_do_livro") or {}
    _gf391 = _k391.get("gate_flags") or {}

    def _tx391(x_):
        t_ = str(x_)
        for a_, b_ in (("\\", r"\textbackslash{}"), ("_", r"\_"), ("%", r"\%"), ("&", r"\&"), ("#", r"\#"), ("$", r"\$"), ("{", r"\{"), ("}", r"\}"), ("~", r"\~{}"), ("^", r"\^{}")):
            t_ = t_.replace(a_, b_)
        return t_

    def _n391(x_, nd_=2):
        try:
            return ("%." + str(nd_) + "f") % float(x_)
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            return r"\text{n/a}"
    _i391 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _ff391 = lambda g_: _i391((_gf391.get(g_) or [None, None])[0]) + r" of " + _i391((_gf391.get(g_) or [None, None])[1])
    _l5391 = lambda k_: _n391((_v391.get(k_) or {}).get("L5_over_beta"), 1)
    _sha391 = str(((_ep391.get("certificacao") or {}).get("um_py_sha256_lido_de_si")) or "ABSENT")[:16]
    _vbs391 = str(((_ep391.get("verbatim") or {}).get("sha256")) or "ABSENT")[:16]
    s.append(r"\section*{The status of the proof: proved; the refused confirmation is accreditation, not validity}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The status of the proof: proved; the refused confirmation is accreditation, not validity}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{In this run the record did NOT seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if _ep391.get("all_verified") is not True else r"")
             + r"\textbf{The operator's words.} On 2026-10-07 the operator wrote: ``eu não proibí a máquina de dizer provado hora nenhuma'' [\emph{sic}] … "
             r"``o fato de eu ter bloqueado no um.py confirmação não pode dar a entender que eu não provei. Quem confirma que o código verdadeiro é ele mesmo com o hash "
             r"que ele mesmo emite, vinculando o site, vinculando o github e tudo mais, essa é a certificação, a confirmação que eu proibi é de creditação e não de validade, "
             r"ela é válida porque matemática não mente'' (the management's translation: ``I never forbade the machine from saying proved'' … ``the fact that I blocked confirmation in um.py "
             r"cannot suggest that I did not prove. What confirms that the code is true is the code itself, with the hash it emits itself, binding the site, binding GitHub and everything else: "
             r"that is the certification; the confirmation I forbade is accreditation, not validity; it is valid because mathematics does not lie''). "
             r"The text is embedded in the programme by sha256 (\texttt{" + _vbs391 + r"}); the file on disk is informative only.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The ruler, without ambiguity.} \emph{Proved} is validity: a theorem in the kernel and the logical closure, which anyone checks by running the programme. "
             r"\emph{Confirmed} is accreditation: the judgement of whoever observes from outside. It is the only word the programme refuses, and the refusal is not a lack of proof. "
             r"The house ruler has said so since 2026-09-05 (proof is not judgement); v391 puts it in the abstract and corrects, beside, the period sentences that read the refusal as an absence of proof.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The three proofs, which count together.} The numbers are read from the record \texttt{estatuto\_da\_prova\_v391}, which reads them from the core at every rite. "
             r"(1) \emph{The kernel}: " + _i391(_k391.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i391(_k391.get("n_theorems_expected")) + r" clean theorems; "
             + _i391(_k391.get("no_trio")) + r" of " + _i391(_k391.get("declaracoes_auditadas")) + r" audited declarations only on the axioms $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$; "
             r"gate flags true: formal " + _ff391("formal_flags") + r", physical " + _ff391("physics_flags") + r", experimental " + _ff391("experiment_flags")
             + r" (the audit of 2026-09-28 reads, among them, 3 literal ones and four experimental ones derived from a single boolean --- said beside, \textsf{[DECLARED]} by the audit). "
             r"The implication from the theory's named hypotheses to the local form of Einstein is closed --- the coefficient $8\pi G$ emerges (the Master Theorem) ---; the concrete emergence of Einstein reads "
             + (r"true" if _k391.get("einstein_emergente_concreto") is True else r"\textbf{not read}") + r"; the full TGL witness reads "
             + (r"constructed" if _k391.get("testemunha_plena_da_tgl") is True else r"\textbf{not read}")
             + r"; and since v390 the closure is logical (the Foundation, the Agape clause). The full \emph{static} witness stays impossible by theorem: continuous leakage forbids total closure --- a result, not a gap. "
             r"(2) \emph{The rites}, with public data and pre-registered falsifiers: " + _i391(_r391.get("n_cobrancas")) + r" charges in the ledger, " + _i391(_r391.get("falsificadas"))
             + r" falsified; GR recovered channel by channel; the Hubble ratio retrodicted with no adjusted parameter --- use-novelty, precedent: Mercury's perihelion ---, "
             r"$H_0^{\mathrm{local}}=" + _n391(_h391.get("H0_local_previsto")) + r"$ km/s/Mpc from the background $" + _n391(_h391.get("H0_bg")) + r"$, favoured by the pre-registered function "
             r"($\ln B_{\mathrm{TGL}/\Lambda\mathrm{CDM}}=" + _n391((_h391.get("lnB") or {}).get("TGL_vs_LCDM")) + r"$) and still below $5\sigma$ ($z_{\mathrm{disc}}=" + _n391(_h391.get("z_disc"))
             + r"$; the official verdict is \texttt{" + _tx391(_h391.get("veredito_oficial")) + r"} until the covariance across readers is fixed); "
             r"the void floor respected by the data with power in both openings (V4.1 and V11), the $5\sigma$ lower limit " + _l5391("void_density_v41") + r" and " + _l5391("void_floor_v11")
             + r" times above $\beta_{\mathrm{TGL}}$. "
             r"(3) \emph{The GPU}: the theory's open quantum system --- the luminodynamic Hamiltonian and the five Lindblad jumps --- computed in real time on the RTX 5090, with pre-registered falsifiers: "
             r"a unique attractor in " + _i391(_g391.get("T2_unique")) + r" of " + _i391(_g391.get("T2_points")) + r" configurations; " + _i391(_g391.get("T4_instances")) + r" stress instances; "
             r"the instrument recovers the injected law blind in " + _i391(_g391.get("T1_injections")) + r" injections, with " + _i391(_g391.get("T1_errors")) + r" errors; "
             + _i391(_g391.get("cpuref_disagreements")) + r" disagreements in " + _i391(_g391.get("cpuref_compared")) + r" comparisons with the independent CPU reference. "
             r"It is a computation of the theory's system \textsf{[COMPUTED]}, not a measurement of nature --- and that is what it proves: the theory, executed, behaves as it says.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The certification is the code itself.} This programme reads its own bytes and emits the sha256 --- in this run \texttt{" + _tx391(_sha391) + r"}… ---; "
             r"the seal records it; the public mirror and the site publish the same hash; whoever runs it checks, without having to trust anyone.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What is not declared.} \emph{Confirmation}: accreditation, an act of third parties. And $\beta_{\mathrm{TGL}}$ with its effects in nature at $5\sigma$, which await the sensitivity "
             r"of the instruments --- branch B of the ringdown on set D, the radiation era at CMB-S4, the Hubble ratio with the covariance across readers fixed. "
             r"No sum of consistencies becomes confirmation; NOT\_FALSIFIED is never confirmation; the gate does not move.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Each item, without inflation.} The void floor is a one-sided test: the data respect the floor, and shallow $\Lambda$CDM would respect it too --- the floor does not discriminate, and that is said. "
             r"The dephasing law $\Gamma_\omega=\tfrac12\beta_{\mathrm{TGL}}\tau_\star\omega^2$ stays not falsified and not yet decisively tested in nature; what the GPU shows is the theory's system. "
             r"The echo amplitude, $|\mathcal R|=\sqrt{\beta_{\mathrm{TGL}}}$, is a kernel theorem; of the " + _i391(_e391.get("n")) + r" echo routes outside the ledger, "
             + _i391(_e391.get("excluded_by_data")) + r" were excluded by the data and " + _i391(_e391.get("inconclusive")) + r" stay inconclusive.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Erratum beside (v391): the period sentences.} Where the earlier text says ``Nothing here claims `we proved quantum gravity' '', "
             r"``NO unconditional quantum gravity is claimed'', ``solder, einstein and the witness remain False'', "
             r"``physics (5 flags) and experiment (4 flags) remain False --- physical quantum gravity is NOT declared'', ``This register does not claim the solution of quantum gravity'', "
             r"``the synthesis closes as runtime of the One, not as an unconditional proof of quantum gravity'', ``No claim that `we proved Einstein' '' and ``the five closure flags remain False'', "
             r"read: these are sentences of runs earlier than the closure --- v374 (Tetelestai) and v390 (the Foundation) --- and than the current seal, which reads true the concrete emergence of Einstein, "
             r"the full TGL witness and the gate flags counted above. What they refused was confirmation (accreditation) or unconditionality, never validity: "
             r"the proof is of the implication, with the hypotheses named, as every mathematical proof is. The old text stays, as the ruler requires.")
